Summary: (i) the alpha-odd term -alpha sin(2 alpha)/l_u of calF^mod obstructs an analytic continuation of l^* in kappa;
         (ii) the alpha-even part l^E(kappa) continues analytically through (1, l_*) and passes EXACTLY through every
              even-N threshold ring (to 40 digits, N = 8..128);
         (iii) odd-N threshold rings miss l^E by 2 pi (varsigma_o - varsigma_e)/N^2 + O(N^-4) (critical mode q = pi - pi/N);
         (iv) hence l_N = l*_cont(kappa_N) + O(N^-4) holds (exactly) for even N with l*_cont = l^E and fails at O(N^-2) for odd N.
OVERALL PASS
